SUMMARY:Building Something That Endures: Roy Williams on Teams\, Talent\, and Leadership
DESCRIPTION:The Wake Forest University Center for Private Business presents a moderated conversation with three-time national championship coach Roy Williams. Drawing from more than three decades of building successful programs\, Williams will share insights on recruiting talent\, sustaining culture\, and leading through change. The event is open to the public and will take place at Kimmel Arena on the UNC Asheville campus. Click here to register. \nVisitor Parking Notice\nVisitors are required to register their vehicles to park on campus. Please visit the UNC Asheville Visitor Parking Permit Registration website to obtain a temporary parking permit. Event signage will be posted to guide visitors to parking areas near the event location. \n\nAccessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/building-something-that-endures-roy-williams-on-teams-talent-and-leadership/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Event-Calendar-TEMPLATE-11.png
