SUMMARY:Choosing Peace After Loss: Israel/Palestine\, Civil Discourse\, and the Courage to Listen
DESCRIPTION:The UNC Asheville Center for Jewish Studies presents Aziz Abu Sarah\, co-author of “The Future Is Peace: A Shared Journey Across the Holy Land.” Drawing from his experiences and work in peacebuilding\, Abu Sarah will explore nonviolence\, dialogue\, shared humanity\, and the possibility of choosing peace after profound loss. \nThe presentation will be followed by a book signing. This event is free and open to the public and will take place in the Blue Ridge Room of Highsmith Student Union. \nClick here to register for this event. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Accessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/choosing-peace-after-loss-israel-palestine-civil-discourse-and-the-courage-to-listen/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Event-Calendar-TEMPLATE-11.png
END:VEVENT
